            { t: "scripture", ref: "Luke 1:11–15", v: "And there appeared unto him an angel of the Lord standing on the right side of the altar of incense. And when Zacharias saw him, he was troubled, and fear fell upon him. But the angel said unto him, Fear not, Zacharias: for thy prayer is heard; and thy wife Elisabeth shall bear thee a son, and thou shalt call his name John. And thou shalt have joy and gladness; and many shall rejoice at his birth. For he shall be great in the sight of the Lord, and shall drink neither wine nor strong drink; and he shall be filled with the Holy Ghost, even from his mother's womb." },
            { t: "p", v: "This is the picture: when Zechariah was burning incense on the altar, the angel Gabriel appeared. It was the time of the evening sacrifice — the time of prayer — and before they began the prayer, they burned incense. The Bible said the angel stood on the right side of the altar of incense." },
            { t: "prayer", v: "Today I pray for you — may your altar carry the incense and the fire of God. May your prayer be carried into the altar of heaven. By the power of the Holy Ghost, your altar will never go down. The fire on your altar will never go out. Your altar will stand tall against every demonic altar, and through you, doors of opportunity will open for family members and loved ones in the name of Jesus." },
            { t: "p", v: "Some of us, the reason we are not having encounters is because the altar has broken down. There is no fire, there is no sacrifice on the altar — so there is no angelic visitation when we cry out for help." }
